On $CC^n$ the inner product is
$ iprod(vb(z), vb(w)) = sum_(i=1)^n overline(z_i) w_i. $
It is Hermitian, $iprod(vb(z), vb(w)) = overline(iprod(vb(w), vb(z)))$; linear in the second argument and anti-linear in the first, $iprod(mu vb(z), vb(w)) = overline(mu) iprod(vb(z), vb(w))$; and positive definite, $iprod(vb(z), vb(z)) = sum_j abs(z_j)^2 >= 0$ with equality iff $vb(z) = vb(0)$. These axioms define an inner product on any vector space over $RR$ or $CC$.
